# ══ THE TWOW TAIL — TWoW-exclusive rows, off the player's chain ════════════════════════════
# Everything from here to LFT is TWoW's own addition — the rows its FrameXML.toc appends after
# its last stock row (ClassTrainerFrameTemplates.xml, its l.93), in its own internal order. Our
# seat is after the last CHAIN row above (TutorialFrame.xml) and before GameMenuFrame.xml,
# which stays last on purpose: in TWoW's toc these load after ALL stock rows, and the game menu
# is ours. The host surface the whole block needs was bound above it; the two genuine gaps it
# had are host verbs now (`StopMusic`, for Everlook's mute button; `CameraZoomOut`, for the
# barbershop's chair-side camera). StatsFrame.xml — the one row this header used to defer as
# living in the lettered-patch merge, not yet extracted — is on the manifest since the full
# chain extraction landed: at its own toc line's seat beside ItemButtonTemplate.xml, with
# `GetDebugStats` bound beside `GetFramerate` to cover its one host call.

# Hooks.lua (its l.95): TWoW's tooltip hooks — `GameTooltip:SetBagItem` / `:SetUnit` wrapped for
# the gear-inspection pass TWoW runs, with a hidden HooksScanTooltip doing the set-bonus scan
# and a SetTalent hook alongside. Pure hooking over the kit far above; no frames, no new host
# surface.
Interface\FrameXML\Hooks.lua
# ChronoboonTimers.lua (its l.96): the world-buff suspend/restore tracker — CHAT_MSG_SYSTEM's
# "Suspended"/"Restored" pair, plus the chronoboon's own bag-item tooltip line (item 83001)
# via a PLAYER_LOGIN hook. Reads chat, hooks a tooltip; nothing else.
Interface\FrameXML\ChronoboonTimers.lua
